Here's a straightforward approach using the concept of divisors and the property that any integer x can be expressed as a product of its prime factors. If we can find all prime factors of x, we can calculate all pairs (a, b) that satisfy the equation a - a (in which a and b are co-prime) and then validate them based on the equation.

